  <title id="bdl29tailbehavior-title">Survival function of a unit after 1, 3 and 10 layers on a log scale</title>
  <desc id="bdl29tailbehavior-desc">Three panels with a logarithmic vertical axis labelled Proportion, from 10 to the minus 6 up to 1, and a horizontal axis from 0 to 10. Solid line: empirical survival function of a unit. Dotted line: the theoretical Weibull tail, a straight line on this axis. After 1 layer the survival function is itself a straight line, above the dotted line. After 3 layers it falls quickly at first and then bends into a straight tail close to the Weibull line. After 10 layers it drops steeply near zero and then decays slowly, staying above the Weibull line.</desc>
